WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.610
A parent asked me: how did the

2
00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:03.990
class do in the maths test?

3
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.060
I had nine marks in front of me.

4
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.240
I could not read all nine to every parent.

5
00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.800
I needed one fair number.

6
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.640
Today: three kinds of middle, and

7
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:17.540
how to measure the spread.

8
00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.130
The mean is what everyone would get

9
00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.950
if we shared the total equally.

10
00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.050
Add all the marks, then divide

11
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:27.310
by how many there are.

12
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.220
Our nine marks add to one hundred and

13
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.720
sixteen, so the mean is about thirteen.

14
00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.220
The median is the middle mark when

15
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:38.400
you line them up in order.

16
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.020
With nine marks, it is the fifth one.

17
00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.700
Here, the median is thirteen.

18
00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:47.590
The mode is the mark that

19
00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:48.790
appears most often.

20
00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:52.010
Here, twelve and fourteen both appear

21
00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.210
twice, so there are two modes.

22
00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:56.920
The mode is handy for things you

23
00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:59.400
cannot add, like favourite colours.

24
00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:01.110
Now watch.

25
00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:04.360
One pupil was ill and scored zero.

26
00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:07.360
The mean drops to about eleven.

27
00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:10.320
The median only moves to twelve.

28
00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:13.170
One extreme mark pulls the mean,

29
00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:15.170
but hardly moves the median.

30
00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:18.510
A middle alone is not enough.

31
00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:22.260
Two classes can have the same mean, but

32
00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:25.540
one has marks from nine to sixteen, and

33
00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.460
the other from two to twenty.

34
00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.840
The range, highest minus

35
00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.620
lowest, shows the spread.

36
00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:33.460
Quick check!

37
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.180
Most pupils get a little pocket

38
00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:38.720
money, but one gets a lot.

39
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.420
Which middle describes a

40
00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:42.740
typical pupil best?

41
00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:44.500
The median.

42
00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.600
The one big amount pulls the mean up, so

43
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.680
the mean looks richer than most pupils

44
00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:51.000
are.

45
00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:54.420
The median stays with the typical pupil.

46
00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.350
In the app, open The

47
00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.550
middle and the spread.

48
00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.660
Drag one pupil's mark from zero to

49
00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:03.460
twenty, and watch the mean,

50
00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:05.960
median, mode and range react.

51
00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:07.850
Your turn.

52
00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.140
A class has a range of eighteen marks.

53
00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:13.700
What does that tell you about the class?

54
00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.940
The marks are very spread out.

55
00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:20.050
Remember: the mean shares out,

56
00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:22.950
the median is the middle, the

57
00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.830
mode is the most common.

58
00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:28.040
And always give a spread with your middle.

59
00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:32.080
Try it yourself: ask ten friends how

60
00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.320
many minutes they walk to school.

61
00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:36.170
Work out the mean, the median

62
00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:38.290
and the range, and say which

63
00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:40.010
middle describes them best.
